  "body": "spec: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#file-upload-state-(type=file)\r\nWebkit and Chrome do not fire `change` event when a file with same filename (from same filepath) is selected again. \r\nFor long time, I thought because if the filename is the same, it is not `change` but reading the spec text, maybe `change` event should be fired every time user selects file on prompt(?) \r\nPerhaps add clarification on what is `change` event. \r\n\r\n[case]\r\nscreen recording: https://youtu.be/B6Ypt9wPuDs\r\n1. [input]select file1 on <input type=\"file\"> \r\n  => input and change event are fired\r\n2. [input]select file1 again\r\n  =>  input and change event is NOT fired\r\n3. Delete the file1, rename file2 to same name as file1\r\n4. [input]select file2 (same file name as file1) \r\n  =>  input and change event is NOT fired\r\n\r\nChromium bug : https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=856911\r\nWebkit bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=187084\r\n\r\nFirefox fires `change` event on every prompt, and I believe this is the most desirable behavior when writing web apps.",
